    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d232">

                <pb facs="0335" n="223" xml:id="pg223"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/5581: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Tenney</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-11-05T16:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 5,
                                1919, 4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received November 6, 7:45
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>[From Harris at Omsk:]</p>
                <p>457. General Dietrichs has resigned as commander of Siberian Army and has been
                    succeeded by General Sakharoff. General Kappel has been placed in charge of
                    third army.</p>
                <p>Weather has turned extremely cold. To-day thermometer registers 15° below zero
                    Reaumur. Since occupation of Petropavlovsk by Bolsheviki practically no change
                    in military operations. Preparations for evacuation of Omsk by diplomatic and
                    military missions now actively progressing.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Tenney</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
